Date: Sat, 19 Dec 2015 01:01:26 +0000
Subject: changing line colors in plots
Message-ID: <Eq1YVbp__1E.N9e3KltADwAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/Eq1YVbp__1E/m/N9e3KltADwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone,

I am preparing graphs to submit for publication and am having difficulty setting the colors for the curves in the graph.

I have figured out how to make a nice black and white 'trace' graph using the following code:

plot(fit.pre,
     type='trace',
     facet_items=T,
     par.strip.text=list(cex=.75),
     par.settings = list(
         fontsize=list(text=16),
         superpose.line = list(col="black",lwd=1),    # <-- This changes color of line from blue to black
         strip.border=list(col="black"),
         strip.background=list(col="gray95")),
     layout=c(4,6),
     theta_lim=c(-3,3),
     auto.key=F,
     aspect=0.6666,
     main="")

However, when I use the same settings to make an 'infotrace' graph, all the information curves are blue.

Can anyone suggest a solution?

Thank you.

Steven

From ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com  Sat Dec 19 01:48:17 2015
From: ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com (Phil Chalmers)
